{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pulls/183","id":4477072625,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQmfsR88AAAABCtq08Q","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/183","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/183.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/183.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/183","number":183,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix all open pipeline issues","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes every open issue at the time of writing — 25 in total, each with tests, delivered as a series of focused commits.\n\nCloses #154, closes #155, closes #156, closes #157, closes #159, closes #160, closes #164, closes #165, closes #166, closes #167, closes #168, closes #169, closes #170, closes #171, closes #172, closes #173, closes #174, closes #175, closes #176, closes #177, closes #178, closes #179, closes #180, closes #181, closes #182\n\n## What changed, by theme\n\n**False-green gates made real**\n- The pipeline status gate now runs in all five workflows (#167), and `check-pipeline-status.sh` distinguishes a superseded run from a genuine timeout by resolving the branch head (#167). Gate job lists are verified against the actual workflow rather than hand-maintained (#175).\n- `detect-code-changes.mjs` classifies a pull request by the whole push (before..after) instead of the last commit, widening to the full PR diff whenever the previous head cannot be proven tested via the Actions API (#156).\n- The jscpd duplication check analyses real JavaScript files now that `format` names languages; threshold set to 10 above the measured 7.35% (#157).\n- The husky `prepare` script verifies `core.hooksPath` after husky runs, since husky exits 0 for every failure (#166).\n- `validate-docs` checks required README section content, not just file existence (#173).\n\n**Release path hardened**\n- command-stream's `$` resolves on non-zero exit, so release scripts enable `shell.errexit(true)` and their catches actually catch (#170).\n- A prettier --check gate runs on staged files before the version commit (#171).\n- `release-preflight` proves NPM_TOKEN/DOCKERHUB_TOKEN work before the 30-minute build, not after it (#176, #181).\n- The package manager declaration is validated and deno.lock is reconciled with it (#154).\n\n**Transient-failure resilience**\n- The fresh-merge fetch retries with backoff (#169).\n- The setup-npm tarball download retries and extracts from a file, so a truncated transfer cannot leave a half-populated npm directory (#168).\n- The budget wrapper escalates to SIGKILL when a command ignores SIGTERM, tracks the process group, and rejects a non-numeric poll interval (#164).\n- The link checker re-checks unanswered URLs through a second method (#182, #159 paths filter).\n\n**Scanner/pinning correctness**\n- `persist-credentials: false` on every checkout (#179, #160).\n- zizmor version pinned and documented correctly; hash-pinned container images; actionlint pinned to a version that understands modern runner labels (#178, #177, #172, #155).\n- Docker buildx GHA cache exchanges carry an explicit scope (#165).\n- Job budget collection honours step `if:` conditions and variable budgets (#180).\n\n**Gate scope**\n- File line limits walk the tracked file list (#174); gate change detection uses ls-files output (#174) and required docs are covered (#173).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm test`: 450 tests, all passing across the node/bun/deno matrix\n- `npm run lint`: clean\n- `npx prettier --check`: clean\n- actionlint (pinned digest): clean\n- zizmor (default + pedantic/high-confidence passes): no findings\n- `npm run check:duplication`: measures 7.35% against threshold 10\n\n## Changeset\n\n`.changeset/fix-all-open-pipeline-issues.md` (patch) is included, so the release pipeline can cut the version.","created_at":"2026-09-08T17:53:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:40:51Z","closed_at":"2026-09-08T20:40:51Z","merged_at":"2026-09-08T20:40:51Z","merge_commit_sha":"c3a6d23b693972a70097430f01e69fcee5a51ad2","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pulls/183/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pulls/183/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/183/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/statuses/e44f5104df132158a348850d6db39a381d5c2373","head":{"label":"link-foundation:fix-all-open-pipeline-issues","ref":"fix